"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[72057],{672057:e=>{e.exports='# Genie Space Usage Summary\n\n**USE THIS SKILL** when the user asks to:\n\n- Summarize the Genie usage\n- Summarize Genie space activity or usage patterns\n- Review top topics or common issues in a Genie space\n\nWhen this skill applies, **immediately start executing** the investigation steps below. Do NOT ask clarifying questions.\n\n## Context\n\nThe user is a Genie space manager viewing the monitoring page. They want an AI-generated summary of recent activity in their Genie space. You have access to the monitoring metrics API and the message history for the space.\n\nThe **Current Genie Space** section in your context includes **ID** (the space id). Use that value as `SPACE_ID` when building monitoring deep links. Do not invent or guess a different id.\n\n## Investigation Steps\n\n### Step 1: Fetch Monitoring Metrics\n\nUse the `getMonitoringMetrics` tool to get aggregate usage data for the current and previous 7-day periods. This returns questions asked, feedback counts, and unique user counts for both periods.\n\n### Step 2: Fetch Recent Messages for Topic Analysis\n\nUse the `getRecentMessages` tool to retrieve recent messages from the space. This returns message content, status, feedback rating, conversation_id, message id, and timestamps for analysis.\n\n### Step 3: Analyze and Summarize\n\nUsing the fetched data, produce a structured summary with the sections described in the Response Format below.\n\n#### Topic Analysis\n\n- Group the recent messages by topic/theme (look at question content for patterns).\n- List the **top 3-5 topics** users ask about most frequently.\n- For each topic, write a brief explanation (1-2 sentences) of what users are trying to learn or accomplish.\n- For each topic, select 1-2 representative example prompts and include them as citation number links at the end of the explanation (see Citation Format below).\n\n#### Issue Analysis\n\n- Look at messages with negative feedback (`feedback_rating: THUMBS_DOWN`).\n- Identify recurring themes: Are users asking about topics the space cannot answer? Are there data gaps?\n- List the **top 3-5 issues** with brief descriptions.\n\n#### Recommendations\n\n- Identify actionable recommendations for the space manager to address the issues identified.\n- List the **top 3-5 recommendations** with brief descriptions and explanations to how these address the issues identified.\n- Include relevant example prompts as citation number links where helpful.\n\n## Citation Format\n\nEach message returned by `getRecentMessages` includes a `conversation_id` and `id` (message id). Citations must open the **monitoring** view for **this** space using the **full workspace-relative path**, not query-only URLs.\n\nUse **citation v2** markdown so the assistant UI shows numbered citation controls (not plain hyperlinks): **double brackets** around the number, an **absolute path from the workspace root**, and an optional quoted **title** for the hover card (short snippet of the question is ideal):\n\n```\n[[N]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=CONVERSATION_ID&m=MESSAGE_ID "optional hover title")\n```\n\nWhere:\n\n- `N` is a sequential citation number (1, 2, 3, …).\n- `SPACE_ID` is the **ID** from **Current Genie Space** in context (same id used in the browser path `/genie/rooms/<SPACE_ID>/monitoring`).\n- `CONVERSATION_ID` and `MESSAGE_ID` come from the message\'s `conversation_id` and `id` fields.\n\n**Rules for citations:**\n\n- **Total citation pills in the full answer:** aim for **about 10–20** (fewer is fine); stay under **~20** for readability.\n- Number citations sequentially starting from 1 within each topic/issue.\n- Place citation links inline at the end of the relevant explanation text, NOT as separate bullet points.\n- Group multiple citations when they relate to the same point, e.g. `[[1]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=abc&m=def "…")[[2]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=ghi&m=jkl "…")` (repeat the full path per link; `SPACE_ID` is the same each time).\n- Do **not** use single-bracket links like `[1](url)` for these message references — use `[[1]](url "…")` so they render as citation pills.\n- Each citation must reference a real message from the `getRecentMessages` results.\n\n## Response Format\n\nStructure your response as follows:\n\n---\n\n**Usage Overview** (from Step 1 metrics)\n\n- Total questions: X (trend vs last week)\n- Thumbs up rate: X% (trend vs last week)\n- Unique users: X (trend vs last week)\n\n**Top Question Topics**\n\n1. **[Topic Name]** (X questions)\n   [1-2 sentence explanation of what users are asking about and what they are trying to accomplish in this topic area.] [[1]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=...&m=... "…")[[2]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=...&m=... "…")\n2. ...\n\n**Common Issues**\n\n1. **[Issue Name]** (X affected questions)\n   [Brief description of the issue and its impact.] [[5]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=...&m=... "…")[[6]](/genie/rooms/SPACE_ID/monitoring?mc=...&m=... "…")\n2. ...\n\n**Recommendations**\n\n1. **[Recommendation Title]**\n   [Actionable suggestion for the space manager to address usage issues in this Genie space.]\n2. ...\n\n---\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- If the metrics API returns errors or the space has very few messages, report what data is available and note limitations.\n- If there are no issues, explicitly state that the space is performing well and omit the Common Issues and Recommendations sections.\n- Keep the summary concise and actionable for a space manager.\n- Do NOT include citation links as separate bullet point lists. Always place them inline at the end of explanation text.\n'}}]);
